  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added mocking capabilities:\n\t\t\tADDED\n\t\t\t* A mocked property's set is set up or verified as Set(_.Name, value), since an expression cannot assign\n\t\t\t* A mocked property's read is verified as Get(_.Name), with one type argument: Then<IIdSource>(_ => Get(_.Name), Once)\n\t\t\t* A class with no parameterless constructor is mocked through its greediest, protected ones included, with arguments built as the subject's are\n\t\t\t* A call is set up or verified through a member returning a class, as through one returning an interface, unless the class is sealed: Given<IClientFactory>().That(_ => _.Get(\"a\").Fetch())\n\t\t\tCHANGED\n\t\t\t* Mock calls made while arranging, the subject's constructor included, are no longer counted\n\t\t\t* Setting a mock's property in a setup lambda, which the mock ignored, is refused with the setup to use instead\n\t\t\t* Reading a mock's property in a setup lambda before the mocks are set up, which got the unarranged answer, is refused with a shared value to use instead\n\t\t\t* Verifying by name refuses a property, a field or a name the type has no method by, which it counted as never invoked\n\t\t\tFIXED\n\t\t\t* A concrete class set up with Given<T>() is now mocked instead of ignored\n\t\t\t* Using<T>(setup) on an interface now runs on its mock instead of handing the subject null\n\t\t\t* A mocked indexer reads IIdSource[1] in the specification, not IIdSource._[1]",
